<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Edington</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">878</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Edington was fought in May 878 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wiltshire">Wiltshire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, between the West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guthrum">Guthrum</a>. Months earlier a surprise attack had driven Alfred into hiding in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somerset">Somerset</a> marshes, but he rallied his forces and won a decisive victory. Guthrum accepted baptism and withdrew to East Anglia, and the peace that followed secured the survival of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-edington.jpg" alt="Battle of Edington" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Trish Steel · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ethandunmem.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
